PR #30761 still publishes `71295c0e`. This proposed amendment is `8a2c814d`; it needs Tamir approval before the PR is updated.

With a third `LiteralString` member, the published normalization depended on insertion order: one tuple order accepted a `list[str]` assignment and the other rejected it. The revision checks empty-string coverage once after union insertion, including `LiteralString`, then rebuilds through the existing normalizer. It removes both insertion-time checks and the special merge/reinsertion path.

The rule still requires builtin `str` with only the falsy exclusion. Nonempty fallbacks, additional intersection constraints and subclass-specific cores keep their handling; literal empty receivers retain their LiteralString-specific overloads.

The reported cases fail on published 71295c and pass on the revision. The whole Boolean fixture, core 86, semantic 541 (35 ignored), IDE 1964, all 532 default Markdown fixtures and strict style checks pass. [Qualification](https://app.buildbuddy.io/invocation/1670b6d4-8b0a-47e6-b460-35761f99e9b7).

